# GOLDEN RA RB OVERLAPPING
# GROUND-TRUTH: N1 of SPEC_PRESENCE_MODEL. `reject BTag(jets[0]) >= 1` and
#   `reject BTag(jets[0]) < 1` are complementary REJECTS over a possibly-absent
#   property. A jet with no `btag` key soft-falses BOTH inner comparisons, so
#   BOTH rejects hold and the event is In BOTH regions -> they genuinely
#   OVERLAP, and for NO other event (no real number is both < 1 and >= 1).
#
#   The witness is therefore an ABSENCE event, and the realizer now builds one:
#   the model reads `defined(jets[0].btag) = 0`, the realizer OMITS the key,
#   and the interpreter accepts the result into both regions. Before the
#   presence model the realizer wrote a fixed property set unconditionally, so
#   this witness was literally unrepresentable.
#
#   THIS PIN MUST NEVER BECOME DISJOINT. Until 2026-07-25 it WAS shipped as
#   PROVEN DISJOINT, solver-less, through the interval fast path, with
#   `refutations: 0` - the first known shipping false PROVEN since the
#   merge-path fixes. Under the presence model both regions encode the shared
#   disjunct `p_btag < 1`, so a common model always exists and no refutation
#   is derivable. The pt cut is what makes `jets[0]` real for the realizer.

object jets
  take Jet
  select pt > 30

region RA
  select size(jets) >= 1
  reject BTag(jets[0]) >= 1

region RB
  select size(jets) >= 1
  reject BTag(jets[0]) < 1
